== Trivia ==
* An athame is a ceremonial blade, generally with a black handle. It is the main ritual implement or magical tool among several used in the religion of [[wikipedia:Wicca|Wicca]] and is also used in various other neopagan witchcraft traditions. The athame stands as one of the four elemental tools in Wicca, traditionally standing for fire.
* A black-handled knife called an athame appears in certain versions of the [[wikipedia:Key of Solomon|Key of Solomon]], a grimoire originating in the Middle Ages.

